555
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:42,660
Not today.

556
00:44:43,420 --> 00:44:46,100
Have you and Dutch talked about how we're gonna get out of this?

557
00:44:46,380 --> 00:44:51,900
I was just discussing with Herr Strauss when the weather breaks, I suppose we'll have to keep heading east.

558
00:44:52,060 --> 00:44:52,420
East?

559
00:44:52,720 --> 00:44:53,480
Into all that?

560
00:45:06,670 --> 00:45:11,490
That civilization... Nothing scarier than that.

561
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:22,660
We found shelter and been resting here in some old abandoned mining town while we wait the thaw.

562
00:45:23,980 --> 00:45:26,640
Hardly the spring I had been hoping for.

563
00:45:30,880 --> 00:45:32,100
Man, alright.

564
00:45:32,960 --> 00:45:36,140
Events in interesting locations are noted in your journal as you explore.

565
00:45:36,320 --> 00:45:37,180
Hold ye to view it.

566
00:45:44,110 --> 00:45:45,810
I actually knew there was a journal in this game.

567
00:45:47,170 --> 00:45:47,830
It's awesome.

568
00:45:48,330 --> 00:45:49,290
Okay, hold on, someone's talking.

569
00:46:23,790 --> 00:46:25,410
We got this.

570
00:46:26,070 --> 00:46:27,270
We're safe.

571
00:46:29,190 --> 00:46:30,950
Stay strong, Jose.

572
00:46:34,120 --> 00:46:35,520
What about you, Arthur?

573
00:46:36,020 --> 00:46:37,080
You doubting me too?

574
00:46:37,600 --> 00:46:37,940
Never.

575
00:46:38,880 --> 00:46:39,220
Good.

576
00:46:40,020 --> 00:46:41,340
Because you know me, son.

577
00:46:41,900 --> 00:46:43,300
I'm just getting started.

578
00:46:44,220 --> 00:46:50,880
Once we get some money, well, they... they better send some good men after us, because they ain't never gonna find us.

579
00:46:51,400 --> 00:46:53,060
But we need money.

580
00:46:53,900 --> 00:46:54,600
Of course, Dutch.

581
00:46:55,880 --> 00:46:58,440
Thank you, son, for your strength.

582
00:46:59,040 --> 00:47:00,460
It means a lot to me.

583
00:47:03,680 --> 00:47:07,400
Dude, he seems so different compared to the first game.

584
00:47:07,560 --> 00:47:10,520
He seemed like a wild man in that first game.

585
00:47:12,320 --> 00:47:14,500
But we know he wasn't always like that, right?

586
00:47:15,140 --> 00:47:22,780
I mean, we know that John learned to read and write because Dutch taught him and stuff like that, you know?

587
00:47:23,280 --> 00:47:24,680
Almost like a father to him.

588
00:47:25,300 --> 00:47:29,040
It's so weird, man, seeing these people sit.

589
00:47:31,380 --> 00:47:31,860
Oh?

590
00:47:32,680 --> 00:47:34,240
Oh, you wanted to sit over here instead?

591
00:47:34,740 --> 00:47:35,400
Okay, that's fine.

592
00:47:36,160 --> 00:47:37,440
Let me check out this journal thing.

593
00:47:38,920 --> 00:47:40,940
Oh, I can look at it while sitting.

594
00:47:41,080 --> 00:47:41,640
I love that.

595
00:47:41,780 --> 00:47:42,280
I love that.

596
00:47:43,440 --> 00:47:43,880
Blackwater.

597
00:47:44,500 --> 00:47:47,980
Dude, I remember the freaking layout of Blackwater.

598
00:47:48,480 --> 00:47:49,320
That's crazy.

599
00:47:50,280 --> 00:47:51,900
That's exactly what it looked like.

600
00:47:52,680 --> 00:47:55,120
But I guess this is Blackwater ten years ago or so.

601
00:47:56,340 --> 00:47:58,560
So the town hall or whatever in the top there.

602
00:47:58,680 --> 00:47:59,680
The river on the right.

603
00:48:01,100 --> 00:48:01,620
Yeah.

604
00:48:03,140 --> 00:48:06,040
Dude, it actually feels like yesterday I played Red Dead 1.

605
00:48:07,580 --> 00:48:08,620
Even though it's not.

606
00:48:11,320 --> 00:48:11,840
Damn.

607
00:48:13,780 --> 00:48:14,880
This guy can draw.

608
00:48:15,700 --> 00:48:16,440
That's nice.

609
00:48:16,560 --> 00:48:17,220
Is that Blackwater?

610
00:48:20,130 --> 00:48:21,150
Oh, here we go.

611
00:48:21,470 --> 00:48:26,450
I bought this new journal after the last one got destroyed in that fire all those months ago.

612
00:48:27,010 --> 00:48:28,070
Whenever it was.

613
00:48:28,870 --> 00:48:34,370
Haven't written or drawn much in the past few months, but I was missing it more than I thought I would.

614
00:48:34,630 --> 00:48:37,730
And finally near a store, so here I am, I guess.

615
00:48:38,430 --> 00:48:46,850
After all that business up north and the fire, we spent a few months in the wilderness, traveling down from the northern grizzlies.

616
00:48:49,650 --> 00:48:50,130
Okay.

617
00:48:50,130 --> 00:48:51,810
Kind of hard to read handwriting.

618
00:48:53,570 --> 00:48:56,230
Stuck mostly in the western foothills of the mountains.

619
00:48:57,290 --> 00:48:59,050
During the worst of the winter.

620
00:48:59,870 --> 00:49:02,190
Food was easy to find and life was good.

621
00:49:02,950 --> 00:49:04,710
Dutch had a lead for some land.

622
00:49:04,910 --> 00:49:06,390
And we were going to buy.

623
00:49:06,690 --> 00:49:09,370
But the land did not match up to his criteria.

624
00:49:09,750 --> 00:49:12,450
Or he got spooked we were being watched by the law.

625
00:49:12,670 --> 00:49:14,430
And that somebody knew who he was.

626
00:49:14,770 --> 00:49:15,990
And we never bought it.

627
00:49:16,590 --> 00:49:18,030
And we are wandering still.

628
00:49:18,970 --> 00:49:21,290
We picked up a couple of new folk in the Grizzlies.

629
00:49:21,670 --> 00:49:22,810
Dude, this is so cool.

630
00:49:22,930 --> 00:49:23,910
I love this system.

631
00:49:24,710 --> 00:49:26,750
Reminds me of The Last of Us, too.

632
00:49:27,450 --> 00:49:28,310
Which I loved.

633
00:49:28,410 --> 00:49:30,050
I loved that journal system in that game.

634
00:49:31,550 --> 00:49:32,450
Okay, who's that?

635
00:49:33,150 --> 00:49:33,410
Jenny.

636
00:49:33,730 --> 00:49:36,530
A sweet young girl we met abandoned on the roadside.

637
00:49:36,810 --> 00:49:37,310
And Micah.

638
00:49:37,530 --> 00:49:39,930
An outlaw Dutch met in a bar someplace.

639
00:49:40,630 --> 00:49:42,810
Dutch seems very taken with Micah.

640
00:49:42,950 --> 00:49:44,330
Who is pretty hot-headed.

641
00:50:00,900 --> 00:50:06,640
So, this is all in the past, right?

642
00:50:06,780 --> 00:50:08,320
Obviously, since he's writing about it.

643
00:50:08,740 --> 00:50:10,200
So, they were in Blackwater.

644
00:50:10,880 --> 00:50:12,240
Something about a boat...

645
00:50:12,300 --> 00:50:12,840
Went down.

646
00:50:13,100 --> 00:50:14,060
It went bad.

647
00:50:14,720 --> 00:50:17,460
And Dutch had to leave a bunch of money and other things behind.

648
00:50:18,880 --> 00:50:20,100
And I guess it's still there.

649
00:50:20,700 --> 00:50:22,320
So we're probably going to come back for that.

650
00:50:26,400 --> 00:50:26,840
Okay?

651
00:50:26,840 --> 00:50:33,600
Unless we're gonna, you know, travel back in time to that, and this is just, like, the prologue, and we're gonna, you know, have flashbacks or something.

652
00:50:34,780 --> 00:50:36,100
I might be onto something.

653
00:50:36,400 --> 00:50:46,280
We got plenty of money, and the trail we took was so torturous and slow, nobody could have followed us south and east, or figured out where we was heading.

654
00:50:46,860 --> 00:50:52,700
We was thinking about California, but then Dutch and Hosea brought us down to Blackwater.

655
00:50:53,320 --> 00:50:54,040
Okay.

656
00:50:57,300 --> 00:50:59,120
These are awesome drawings.

657
00:51:01,040 --> 00:51:02,440
That's kind of cool.

658
00:51:05,580 --> 00:51:06,780
People working away.

659
00:51:08,000 --> 00:51:10,200
He's journaling someone else who's journaling.

660
00:51:10,440 --> 00:51:11,080
That's funny.

661
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:16,900
Blackwater has apparently grown a whole lot since any of them was leased here.

662
00:51:17,100 --> 00:51:17,920
Or last here.

663
00:51:18,340 --> 00:51:20,900
I was told to expect little more than a trading post.

664
00:51:21,220 --> 00:51:22,780
But the place is growing fast.

665
00:51:22,980 --> 00:51:24,540
And it's almost a small city.

666
00:51:24,840 --> 00:51:27,220
The town seems to be riddled with corruption.

667
00:51:27,580 --> 00:51:29,360
But there's certainly plenty of money here.

668
00:51:30,100 --> 00:51:32,500
It's good to be sleeping in a bed from time to time.

669
00:51:32,830 --> 00:51:37,310
And living a mere civilized life after a long... under canvas?

670
00:51:38,950 --> 00:51:39,790
I guess.

671
00:51:40,150 --> 00:51:43,730
But I do not particularly like being this near a town.

672
00:51:44,590 --> 00:51:47,170
Yeah, he seems kind of scared of civilization.

673
00:51:47,790 --> 00:51:48,010
Right?

674
00:51:49,870 --> 00:51:51,190
Scared of change, maybe.

675
00:51:53,610 --> 00:51:55,090
What is that on the left there?

676
00:51:56,110 --> 00:51:57,130
A fireplace?

677
00:51:58,150 --> 00:51:59,210
And some guards?

678
00:52:00,320 --> 00:52:02,920
We are living here, camping outside town mostly.

679
00:52:03,200 --> 00:52:04,940
Hidden in plain sight, I guess.

680
00:52:05,460 --> 00:52:06,700
Life seems pretty easy.

681
00:52:07,520 --> 00:52:09,760
Abigail and Marston keep arguing.

682
00:52:10,140 --> 00:52:12,200
I wonder why exactly he came back.

683
00:52:12,620 --> 00:52:16,360
He cannot seem to decide if he wants to be a father to that boy of his or not.

684
00:52:17,300 --> 00:52:18,600
Oh, shit.

685
00:52:19,800 --> 00:52:20,620
That's right.

686
00:52:21,280 --> 00:52:23,940
In the first game, he did leave for a while, right?

687
00:52:25,060 --> 00:52:28,260
And then he came back and decided to, you know, take care of his family.

688
00:52:28,750 --> 00:52:30,210
And we know what happened after that.

689
00:52:31,050 --> 00:52:35,070
Like he felt guilty about the way he wasn't there for... for his kid.

690
00:52:36,510 --> 00:52:37,330
Oh man.

691
00:52:38,730 --> 00:52:40,250
The arguing is exhausting.

692
00:52:40,710 --> 00:52:44,790
I heard talk of a man sounded like... Trelon?

693
00:52:45,990 --> 00:52:46,550
Freylon?

694
00:52:46,670 --> 00:52:47,250
What does that say?

695
00:52:48,710 --> 00:52:50,930
A man sounded like Trelawney.

696
00:52:51,130 --> 00:52:53,010
But we haven't seen him for many months.

697
00:52:53,610 --> 00:52:54,170
Okay.

698
00:52:57,270 --> 00:52:58,990
Hosea and I are onto something.

699
00:52:59,530 --> 00:53:00,570
Something pretty big.

700
00:53:00,810 --> 00:53:05,470
Might be a lot of cash coming in to do with the real estate scam Hosea thinks he may have discovered.

701
00:53:06,130 --> 00:53:07,350
I'm not sure yet.

702
00:53:08,510 --> 00:53:10,010
The perfect crime, we think.

703
00:53:11,270 --> 00:53:13,550
One where we rob crooks.

704
00:53:13,890 --> 00:53:15,250
We are being real careful.

705
00:53:17,390 --> 00:53:19,330
It's fun working with Hosea again.

706
00:53:19,830 --> 00:53:22,490
The man is an artist of... nonsense.

707
00:53:23,630 --> 00:53:25,170
Even if nothing comes of it...

708
00:53:25,400 --> 00:53:27,080
We are having an amusing enough time.

709
00:53:29,080 --> 00:53:31,300
I have to analyze this to understand what's written.

710
00:53:32,660 --> 00:53:36,100
Is that the boat that they're all talking about?

711
00:53:37,120 --> 00:53:39,380
It's good to be running scams again.

712
00:53:39,940 --> 00:53:41,300
Hosea is a born huckster.

713
00:53:41,560 --> 00:53:48,320
He's getting anxious, worried that by lingering in town, we are going to bring under undue attention on ourselves.

714
00:53:48,740 --> 00:53:51,120
But Dutch thinks he's also onto something big.

715
00:53:51,380 --> 00:53:52,580
His words, not mine.

716
00:53:52,970 --> 00:53:55,370
Bank money being brought in by boat, apparently.

717
00:53:55,870 --> 00:53:57,710
So for now, we are working on both.

718
00:53:59,270 --> 00:54:00,630
Things and seeing what happens.

719
00:54:00,790 --> 00:54:01,090
Oh, okay.

720
00:54:01,410 --> 00:54:01,830
Both things.

721
00:54:02,530 --> 00:54:05,970
Plan is to flee west into the desert country someplace if we can.

722
00:54:08,810 --> 00:54:12,010
Micah and Dutch are planning to rob the ferry in town.

723
00:54:12,390 --> 00:54:13,990
They think it's laden with riches.

724
00:54:14,350 --> 00:54:16,210
Cash coming in for the banks.

725
00:54:16,630 --> 00:54:17,710
Coming in by boat.

726
00:54:18,270 --> 00:54:20,610
For once, I'm not getting involved in the job.

727
00:54:21,090 --> 00:54:25,990
Jose and I are too taken up with our business, which I believe could go very well.

728
00:54:26,390 --> 00:54:31,310
And Dutch seems confident that with the group of... or the group assembled, all will be okay.

729
00:54:32,750 --> 00:54:33,430
All right.

730
00:54:34,010 --> 00:54:38,830
So that's why Dutch was like, we were missing you when they were talking about the boat.

731
00:54:38,970 --> 00:54:40,010
So I wasn't there for that.

732
00:54:41,770 --> 00:54:45,830
Plan is for them to carry out the job, then flee into the wilderness out to the west.

733
00:54:46,300 --> 00:54:49,400
The next day, Hosea and I carry out our own scam and join them.

734
00:54:49,960 --> 00:54:51,560
Dutch seems happy and excited.

735
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:53,640
He's talking again about California.

736
00:54:53,940 --> 00:54:56,080
But he's also talking about a lot of other places.

737
00:54:57,880 --> 00:54:58,360
Right.

738
00:55:00,720 --> 00:55:01,700
Blackwater Saloon.

739
00:55:04,590 --> 00:55:05,270
That's nice.

740
00:55:06,850 --> 00:55:09,270
Is that what the saloon looked like in the first game?

741
00:55:09,750 --> 00:55:11,590
I think it actually did look like this.

742
00:55:13,570 --> 00:55:14,930
Now that I think back on it.

743
00:55:17,450 --> 00:55:18,350
A nice horse.

744
00:55:19,990 --> 00:55:21,830
Oh, Blackwater no-go.

745
00:55:22,790 --> 00:55:24,150
We've been running for weeks.

746
00:55:24,430 --> 00:55:25,670
I mean, running more than usual.

747
00:55:26,070 --> 00:55:30,850
The job they were talking about in Blackwater, robbing that ferry, it turned into a disaster.

748
00:55:40,440 --> 00:55:41,840
Yeah.

749
00:55:54,760 --> 00:55:56,340
Davy T.

750
00:55:57,260 --> 00:56:01,020
Then as we were fleeing east over the grizzlies, an almighty storm hit us.

751
00:56:01,400 --> 00:56:02,740
Oh, so that's what we just saw.

752
00:56:03,660 --> 00:56:09,180
Davy Callender, who got shot in the gut on the road, passed away.

753
00:56:09,540 --> 00:56:10,940
It was brutal to watch.

754
00:56:11,440 --> 00:56:13,940
And the rest of us nearly froze.

755
00:56:14,300 --> 00:56:19,980
But we found shelter and have been resting here in some old abandoned mining town while we await the thaw.

756
00:56:23,100 --> 00:56:24,120
Camp Coulter.

757
00:56:27,400 --> 00:56:28,700
So that's where we are now.

758
00:56:29,780 --> 00:56:31,100
What the hell is going on?

759
00:56:33,920 --> 00:56:35,460
Someone has a bit of trouble.

760
00:56:38,180 --> 00:56:38,900
Choo-choo.

761
00:56:55,020 --> 00:56:55,940
Cowering up here.

762
00:56:56,880 --> 00:56:57,600
Found a girl.

763
00:56:57,840 --> 00:56:59,320
Well, a woman, I should say.

764
00:56:59,920 --> 00:57:03,680
Her husband had been murdered by some of Como Driscoll's boys.

765
00:57:04,340 --> 00:57:05,360
Nasty business.

766
00:57:06,480 --> 00:57:07,520
And that's it.

767
00:57:07,660 --> 00:57:07,940
Okay.

768
00:57:08,280 --> 00:57:08,840
Cool.

769
00:57:10,040 --> 00:57:10,960
Very nice.

770
00:57:11,820 --> 00:57:13,000
There's also chapters.

771
00:57:15,220 --> 00:57:17,660
Oh, because we're in chapter one, or...?

772
00:57:17,660 --> 00:57:18,580
No.

773
00:57:19,060 --> 00:57:19,600
Okay, I'm not sure.

774
00:57:20,380 --> 00:57:20,760
Cool.

775
00:57:21,300 --> 00:57:22,440
That is awesome.

776
00:57:22,900 --> 00:57:24,480
It's gonna get filled out, I guess, as we play.

777
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:27,660
What is he doing?

778
00:57:31,140 --> 00:57:33,320
Oh, he's scribbling in a journal as well, that's cool.

779
00:57:49,850 --> 00:57:53,430
Speaking of John, are we actually not going to play as him at all?

780
00:57:55,030 --> 00:57:56,050
Maybe at some point.

781
00:57:57,250 --> 00:57:58,690
Like, the hell?

782
00:58:00,110 --> 00:58:01,290
It's kind of weird, isn't it?

783
00:58:02,410 --> 00:58:03,450
Can I read that book?

784
00:58:03,590 --> 00:58:03,750
No?

785
00:58:06,320 --> 00:58:06,880
Hosea.

786
00:58:07,000 --> 00:58:07,480
Oh, shit!

787
00:58:08,400 --> 00:58:09,440
How's it going, man?

788
00:58:10,020 --> 00:58:10,880
Resting by the fire.

789
00:58:27,440 --> 00:58:28,580
Man, dude!

790
00:58:29,040 --> 00:58:30,780
Oh my god, this is so good.

791
00:58:31,480 --> 00:58:32,420
Search the drawer.

792
00:58:33,800 --> 00:58:34,360
Nothing.

793
00:58:35,440 --> 00:58:37,800
Oh man, I love this pace.

794
00:58:39,160 --> 00:58:40,300
This is fantastic.

795
00:58:41,700 --> 00:58:43,180
Listen to the sounds outside.

796
00:58:46,900 --> 00:58:47,840
There's someone in here.

797
00:58:48,680 --> 00:58:49,440
Who is that?

798
00:58:52,380 --> 00:58:54,700
Wait, I can go and talk to John, I guess, at some point?

799
00:58:56,160 --> 00:58:56,620
Molly.

800
00:59:03,520 --> 00:59:04,380
Wow, okay.

801
00:59:08,640 --> 00:59:10,060
I have to process that one, huh?

802
00:59:10,680 --> 00:59:11,800
Look at the cobwebs.

803
00:59:11,940 --> 00:59:12,720
Dude, the detail.

804
00:59:13,440 --> 00:59:14,580
I'm not gonna say it.

805
00:59:14,780 --> 00:59:18,200
This looks pretty much as good as Grand Theft Auto 6.

806
00:59:18,460 --> 00:59:19,260
Am I crazy?

807
00:59:19,540 --> 00:59:21,220
How the fuck is this even possible?

808
00:59:22,580 --> 00:59:26,280
Well, I guess I am playing it on PC in 4K and, you know, full framerate and all that.

809
00:59:26,360 --> 00:59:26,680
But still.

810
00:59:27,320 --> 00:59:28,220
Oh my god.

811
00:59:29,920 --> 00:59:31,460
That is wild, bro.

812
00:59:36,240 --> 00:59:37,640
Damn!

813
00:59:37,640 --> 00:59:39,040
Man!

814
00:59:42,970 --> 00:59:44,130
Let me eat something.

815
00:59:44,630 --> 00:59:45,350
What's that?

816
00:59:45,790 --> 00:59:46,970
Oh, the card we found.

817
00:59:48,110 --> 00:59:49,230
Salted beef.

818
00:59:49,490 --> 00:59:50,650
I have a necklace?

819
00:59:51,270 --> 00:59:53,830
A valuable gold pendant necklace can be sold.

820
00:59:56,370 --> 00:59:57,050
Journal.

821
00:59:57,430 --> 00:59:58,970
Oh, I guess that's the one we just looked at.

822
00:59:59,490 --> 01:00:00,510
Premium cigarettes.

823
01:00:00,910 --> 01:00:03,970
Slightly damages stamina core, slightly restores deadeye core.

824
01:00:05,330 --> 01:00:06,470
Mmm, deadeye.

825
01:00:07,030 --> 01:00:08,150
Like me some of that.

826
01:00:09,770 --> 01:00:11,330
Provisions, tonics.

827
01:00:12,200 --> 01:00:13,220
Miracle tonic.

828
01:00:14,220 --> 01:00:15,120
Health cure.

829
01:00:17,540 --> 01:00:19,080
Oh, binoculars!

830
01:00:19,340 --> 01:00:20,000
Thank you, game!

831
01:00:20,760 --> 01:00:23,260
Thank you for giving me binoculars early on.

832
01:00:23,580 --> 01:00:26,960
And not, like, at the end of the game like they did in Red Dead 1.

833
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:28,020
That was such a blunder.

834
01:00:28,420 --> 01:00:29,640
I can't believe it.

835
01:00:30,440 --> 01:00:30,960
Bandana.

836
01:00:31,360 --> 01:00:33,460
Hide your identity while committing crimes!

837
01:00:33,680 --> 01:00:33,980
Okay.

838
01:00:34,660 --> 01:00:35,220
Sweet.

839
01:00:36,840 --> 01:00:37,900
Cigarette cards.

840
01:00:38,260 --> 01:00:38,760
Alright.

841
01:00:39,790 --> 01:00:40,550
Very cool.

842
01:00:43,330 --> 01:00:44,810
Let me see what else I can do in here.

843
01:00:46,710 --> 01:00:48,410
Can I actually keep talking to these people?

844
01:00:54,910 --> 01:00:55,350
Alright.

845
01:01:01,110 --> 01:01:03,610
I think he's tired of me talking to him.

846
01:01:04,030 --> 01:01:06,410
He's busy scribbling in his journal.

847
01:01:08,250 --> 01:01:09,070
Damn.

848
01:01:10,010 --> 01:01:13,910
So I guess this is where I save my game or... or not.

849
01:01:15,910 --> 01:01:16,730
Beautiful.

850
01:01:17,350 --> 01:01:17,810
Beautiful.

851
01:01:21,530 --> 01:01:22,690
What's in here?

852
01:01:24,690 --> 01:01:26,310
That's a freaking grindstone.

853
01:01:26,950 --> 01:01:28,070
And a shovel.

854
01:01:31,220 --> 01:01:32,040
Carpentry tools.

855
01:01:32,540 --> 01:01:33,100
All right.

856
01:01:33,700 --> 01:01:35,220
Abandoned mining town, right?

857
01:01:36,460 --> 01:01:37,140
Oh, man.

858
01:01:37,200 --> 01:01:38,120
It's so bright out here.

859
01:01:38,280 --> 01:01:38,520
Damn.

860
01:01:40,160 --> 01:01:40,500
Ooh.

861
01:01:41,200 --> 01:01:41,720
Wow.

862
01:01:42,000 --> 01:01:42,940
Whoa, man.

863
01:01:43,620 --> 01:01:44,960
This looks so good.

864
01:01:45,520 --> 01:01:46,300
Fucking hell.

865
01:01:48,420 --> 01:01:53,220
Okay, so we got a couple things down that way, but I want to explore all these places here.

866
01:01:55,140 --> 01:01:56,480
There's houses over there, too.

867
01:01:56,620 --> 01:01:57,600
Actually, it looks more...

868
01:01:59,210 --> 01:02:00,090
Abandoned, really.

869
01:02:01,050 --> 01:02:02,270
In disrepair.

870
01:02:06,610 --> 01:02:08,050
Whoa, everyone's in here.

871
01:02:14,070 --> 01:02:15,190
Oh, that's the new girl.

872
01:02:21,610 --> 01:02:24,210
Dude, the fact that I respond to this is crazy good.

873
01:02:24,570 --> 01:02:25,830
It's almost like an RPG.

874
01:02:56,580 --> 01:02:59,160
Is that actually Jack down there?

875
01:02:59,840 --> 01:03:01,300
Oh, it is.

876
01:03:02,200 --> 01:03:03,620
That's so weird.

877
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:11,680
...so impoverished that he hath no oblation, chooseth the tree that will not rot.

878
01:03:12,800 --> 01:03:19,920
He seeketh unto him a cunning workman to prepare a graven image that shall not be moved.

879
01:03:21,040 --> 01:03:22,500
Have ye not known?

880
01:03:22,780 --> 01:03:24,140
Have ye not heard?

881
01:03:24,460 --> 01:03:27,320
Hath it not been told to you from the beginning?

882
01:03:27,960 --> 01:03:33,380
Have ye not understood from the foundations of the earth?

883
01:03:35,140 --> 01:03:52,080
Is it he that sitteth upon the circle of the earth, and the inhabitants thereof are as grasshoppers, that stretcheth out the heavens as a curtain, and spreadeth them out as a tent to dwell in?

884
01:03:53,160 --> 01:04:01,240
That bringeth the princes to nothing, he maketh the judges of the earth as vanity.

885
01:04:01,580 --> 01:04:06,220
Yea, they shall not be planted.

886
01:04:06,660 --> 01:04:09,420
Yea, they shall not be sown.

887
01:04:09,880 --> 01:04:21,600
Yea, their stock shall not take root in the earth, and he shall also blow upon them, and they shall wither, and the whirlwind shall take them away as stubble.

888
01:04:24,180 --> 01:04:30,380
To whom then will ye liken me, or shall I be equal, saith the Holy One?

889
01:04:31,720 --> 01:04:43,880
Lift up your eyes on high, and behold, who hath created these things, that bringeth out their hosts by number, and calleth them all by names, by the greatness of his might.

890
01:04:44,120 --> 01:04:48,340
For that he hath strong in power, not one faileth.

891
01:04:50,160 --> 01:05:00,620
Why sayest thou, O Jacob, and speaketh O Israel, my way is hid from the Lord, and my judgment is passed over from God?

892
01:05:02,360 --> 01:05:03,940
Hast thou not known?

893
01:05:04,440 --> 01:05:13,740
Hast thou not heard that the everlasting God, the Lord, the creator of the ends of the earth, fainteth not, neither is weary?

894
01:05:14,590 --> 01:05:18,810
There is no searching of his understanding.

895
01:05:20,090 --> 01:05:26,750
He giveth power to the faint, and to them that hath no might he increaseth their strength.

896
01:05:27,970 --> 01:05:34,530
Even the youths shall faint and be weary, and the young men shall utterly fail.

897
01:05:35,450 --> 01:05:40,130
But they that wait upon the Lord shall renew their strength.

898
01:05:40,750 --> 01:05:43,870
They shall mount up with wings as eagles.

899
01:05:44,130 --> 01:05:49,630
They shall run and not be weary, and they shall walk... and not think.

900
01:05:58,770 --> 01:05:59,490
Yeah.

901
01:06:07,190 --> 01:06:07,910
Huh.

902
01:06:13,010 --> 01:06:16,670
Yeah, Jesse, what the fuck are you talking about, actually?

903
01:06:17,190 --> 01:06:18,510
Reverend Swanson.

904
01:06:19,250 --> 01:06:20,290
Alright, then.

905
01:06:23,250 --> 01:06:24,090
Thank you for that.

906
01:06:24,890 --> 01:06:25,470
Who are you?

907
01:06:26,830 --> 01:06:27,190
Strauss.

908
01:06:33,950 --> 01:06:39,430
Speaking of, is that him in the back there?

909
01:06:39,550 --> 01:06:40,130
I think it is.

910
01:06:46,850 --> 01:06:48,110
He sounds German to me.

911
01:06:48,910 --> 01:06:50,570
And since his name is Strauss...

912
01:06:50,990 --> 01:06:52,570
I think he may be of German origin.

913
01:06:54,990 --> 01:06:55,710
Susan.

914
01:07:04,210 --> 01:07:06,710
What about Jack?

915
01:07:22,690 --> 01:07:24,330
Oh my god, it's Jack.

916
01:07:25,190 --> 01:07:26,010
Little Jack.

917
01:07:28,910 --> 01:07:29,390
Wait!

918
01:07:31,070 --> 01:07:31,550
Uncle!

919
01:07:32,610 --> 01:07:34,650
That's the guy from the first game at the end.

920
01:07:35,210 --> 01:07:36,070
What the hell, man?

921
01:07:53,740 --> 01:07:58,300
Dude, the fact that I can interact with all these people makes me so happy.

922
01:07:58,760 --> 01:08:01,620
It means they really took their time with this shit, man.

923
01:08:02,000 --> 01:08:04,220
This is gonna be some good stuff, I think.

924
01:08:04,580 --> 01:08:04,860
Tilly.

925
01:08:10,120 --> 01:08:10,600
Right.

926
01:08:14,720 --> 01:08:15,200
Abigail.

927
01:08:27,710 --> 01:08:29,090
Wait a minute, was this like a school?

928
01:08:29,310 --> 01:08:30,090
Look at the blackboard.

929
01:08:32,190 --> 01:08:33,670
Looks like a tiny schoolroom.

930
01:08:34,270 --> 01:08:35,290
Or schoolhouse.

931
01:08:37,150 --> 01:08:37,870
What's up, dude?

932
01:08:39,110 --> 01:08:39,550
John!

933
01:08:52,460 --> 01:08:55,860
Dude, it's so weird seeing John there and not playing him.

934
01:08:56,060 --> 01:08:57,480
You know, hearing his voice?

935
01:08:58,200 --> 01:08:59,180
It's crazy.

936
01:09:01,280 --> 01:09:01,800
Okay.

937
01:09:02,380 --> 01:09:03,980
Well, good catching up, guys.

938
01:09:04,600 --> 01:09:05,460
What was your name again?

939
01:09:06,600 --> 01:09:08,580
Karen, and then we had... who's that?

940
01:09:09,460 --> 01:09:10,420
Mary Beth?

941
01:09:13,630 --> 01:09:16,590
And this one was Sadie.

942
01:09:23,710 --> 01:09:38,650
Yeah, that sucks, I guess.

943
01:09:39,160 --> 01:09:42,780
Seemed like they had a nice thing going there at that place, you know?

944
01:09:43,740 --> 01:09:46,400
Until those boys came by and ruined it all.

945
01:09:46,740 --> 01:09:47,560
Partied for three days.

946
01:09:48,320 --> 01:09:50,880
I still don't understand where the hell she was in there.

947
01:09:50,940 --> 01:09:51,880
Because I was looking everywhere.

948
01:09:52,500 --> 01:09:54,920
I did not find a woman hiding in there.

949
01:09:55,100 --> 01:09:55,900
Maybe she was under the bed.

950
01:09:58,080 --> 01:09:58,480
Damn.

951
01:09:58,920 --> 01:10:00,240
Dude, this looks incredible!

952
01:10:00,760 --> 01:10:02,280
Like, I didn't even have to go in there!

953
01:10:03,300 --> 01:10:04,720
Oh, man, I love it!

954
01:10:05,340 --> 01:10:07,320
This is gonna be some good shit.

955
01:10:08,380 --> 01:10:09,140
Wow.

956
01:10:10,080 --> 01:10:11,680
Let me try these binoculars.

957
01:10:12,880 --> 01:10:15,020
Uh... Like that.

958
01:10:16,320 --> 01:10:17,440
How was it?

959
01:10:25,320 --> 01:10:26,320
Oh, yeah.

960
01:10:27,620 --> 01:10:29,680
Wait, what the hell are those keybinds?

961
01:10:31,620 --> 01:10:32,380
Uh...

962
01:10:35,240 --> 01:10:37,800
I have no idea what those buttons are on my keyboard.

963
01:10:39,980 --> 01:10:40,800
Looks nice, though.

964
01:10:41,200 --> 01:10:43,320
I'm gonna have to... Maybe I'll go through the settings.

965
01:10:44,260 --> 01:10:45,960
And actually change some of these hotkeys.

966
01:10:46,240 --> 01:10:47,520
Because some of them are weird, man.

967
01:10:47,660 --> 01:10:49,180
Like, going back is backspace?

968
01:10:49,720 --> 01:10:50,120
Really?

969
01:10:50,320 --> 01:10:51,020
Of all keys?

970
01:10:51,720 --> 01:10:54,120
I mean, sure, you know, but... Okay.

971
01:10:54,280 --> 01:10:55,380
Guys, I'm gonna take a break here.

972
01:10:55,520 --> 01:10:58,100
This is freaking fantastic.

973
01:10:58,820 --> 01:11:01,940
So far, 10 out of 10 opening to the game.

974
01:11:02,060 --> 01:11:02,440
Wow.

975
01:11:02,830 --> 01:11:04,730
I can't believe how good this game looks.

976
01:11:04,950 --> 01:11:07,530
The voice acting is crazy good.

977
01:11:07,930 --> 01:11:21,750
The quality step-up from the first game, in terms of cutscenes, and just the way characters are moving, how they're animated, and just the general flow of the storytelling, is, like, completely next level.

978
01:11:22,410 --> 01:11:28,590
I actually do not remember when Red Dead Redemption 1 came out, but, like, it must have been...

979
01:11:29,550 --> 01:11:30,870
Many years before this.

980
01:11:31,130 --> 01:11:32,690
